; TEST: expect-exit=200
;
; The vector float group's ARITHMETIC, end to end (ssa-ir.md 2.3's vector
; row, 2.2's vf32.N/vf64.N row): scalars lay each lane's raw IEEE image in
; memory (`fconst` bits + a scalar store), `load vf*.N ... nativus` gathers
; the lanes, one packed vadd/vsub/vmul/vdiv runs one IEEE rounding PER LANE
; in the function's rotundatio (the prelude's MXCSR image, as float_arith.ir
; pins for the scalar group), `store` puts the lanes back, and every check
; reads ONE LANE with a scalar load and compares it against an INDEPENDENTLY
; spelled fconst image -- the computed bits agree with text the fixture wrote
; down, never with the vector side agreeing with itself.
;
; Part 1, vf32.4 -- A = (1.0+2^-23, 2.5, 2.0, 9.0), B = (2^-24, 1.5, 2.0,
; 2.0), all four ops (checks 1-16). Lane 0 of vadd is the rounding-tie pin
; (1.0+2^-23)+2^-24 is EXACTLY between 1.0+2^-23 and 1.0+2^-22: ad_parem
; rounds up to the even mantissa 1.0+2^-22; a toward-zero or toward +inf
; image exits 1. Lane 0 of vsub is the mirror tie, below 1.0+2^-23, rounding
; down to even 1.0. vdiv lane 1 is the inexact one (2.5/1.5 = 5/3).
; Part 2, vf64.2 -- A = (1.0+2^-52, 9.0), B = (2^-53, 2.0) (checks 17-24);
; the same tie pins in f64.
; Part 3, vf32.8 -- A = (1..8), B = (0.5)x8, one vadd (checks 25-32): the
; 32-byte vector is two 16-byte chunks of movups/addps, so this part is what
; proves the second chunk moves at all (a single-chunk lowering exits 25).
;
; Constants below are the exact values, computed with python (Fraction
; round-to-nearest-even), never by hand. Operand images live at slot
; offsets 16..143, result stores at 144..303; everything nativus.
;
; Mutations (run): movups swapped for movaps with an unaligned slot -> the
; emitted program faults, not an exit code (recorded: movu is the contract).
; addps spelled addpd in part 1 -> exit 1 (the tie lane reads garbage).
; The vf64.2 chunk using divsd/pd on the WRONG width -> exit 17 or 18.
; The chunk loop stopping at the first 16 bytes -> part 3 exits 25.
;
; Check k returns k on a mismatch; all 32 right: exit 200.

